    "id": "05-product-map",
    "name": "05-product-map.md",
    "content": "BrightLocal product map — how to interpret lazy vertical prompts.\nWhen a request names a product vertical (\"the hub page for Citations\", \"rankings page\", \"reviews dashboard\"), do NOT invent navigation: use the standard app shell (SidebarProvider > GlobalLayout > GlobalLayoutSidebar > Sidebar with Header/Content/Footer, footer = SidebarAccountDropdown), set isActive on that vertical's nav item, and title the page header for the vertical. Location nav items, in order: Location Summary, AI Insights, Rankings, Local Search Grid, Citations, GBP, Reputation & Reviews.\nResponsive shell: the sidebar hides below lg (the live platform's behaviour). Every app-shell screen must include a mobile top bar as the FIRST child of GlobalLayoutContent: <header className=\"flex items-center gap-1 px-1 py-1 lg:hidden\"><SidebarTrigger dataHook=\"mobile-sidebar-trigger\" className=\"size-11\"><Menu className=\"size-5\" /></SidebarTrigger><Logo className=\"h-6\" dataHook=\"mobile-logo\" /></header>. Keep header padding minimal (px-1): the 44px trigger already carries ~12px internal inset, so the glyph lands ~16px from the screen edge like the live platform — no extra left padding/margin on the trigger itself. The Menu (three-line hamburger, from @brightlocal/icons) matches the live platform; the size-11 (44px) className is the minimum touch target and the size-5 glyph matches the sidebar nav icons. No border-b — the live platform's mobile bar has no dividing line. SidebarTrigger opens the design system's built-in mobile sheet — never hand-roll a drawer.\nDemo persona: the logged-in user in every screen is Andy Smith (andy@acmecorp.com, avatar initials AS) — use exactly this in the SidebarAccountDropdown and anywhere a signed-in user appears.\nSidebar nav icons: lucide icons from @brightlocal/icons at 20px (className=\"size-5\", default strokeWidth) — inside sidebar navigation this overrides the general \"16px\" icon rule. (Deliberate deviation: the live platform ships 24px/strokeWidth 1.33 here, which contradicts its own docs and reads oversized; 20px is our curated middle.) Icon pairings: Your Locations=House, Location Summary=LayoutDashboard, AI Insights=Sparkles, Rankings=TrendingUp, Local Search Grid=Grid3x3, Citations=Link, GBP=Store, Reputation & Reviews=Star, Location Manager=Building, White-label=Globe.\nHub-page conventions per vertical (a hub = score/stat summary row + one primary work surface + one CTA):\n- Citations — citations-found score (e.g. 53/60), listings sync status, directory table (directory name, listing status, NAP accuracy), CTA \"Build Citations\".\n- Rankings — average ranking position, keywords in top 3, search visibility %, tracked-keywords table, CTA \"Run New Audit\".\n- Local Search Grid — geo-grid map as the primary surface, keyword selector, competitor comparison beside it.\n- GBP — profile-completeness score, field-level audit checklist, sync status.\n- Reputation & Reviews — average rating, review velocity, per-site breakdown (Google, Facebook, Yelp), reply queue.\n- Location Summary — the overview dashboard: visibility score, rating, citations and actions-required stat cards."
