    "content": "Local-SEO glossary — use these terms correctly in generated copy:\n- GBP = Google Business Profile (formerly GMB / Google My Business).\n- NAP = Name, Address, Phone — consistency across directories is the core citations quality metric.\n- Citation = any online mention of a business's NAP (directories, apps, map services).\n- SERP = search engine results page; the \"local pack\" is the 3-result map unit at the top.\n- Geo-grid = a map grid of ranking positions sampled at points around a location.\n- SoLV = Share of Local Voice — % of grid points where the business ranks top 3.\n- Review velocity = the rate of new reviews over time.\n- SMS = text message (review-request campaigns send invitations by SMS or email).\nIn UI copy, expand an acronym on first use (\"Google Business Profile (GBP)\"), then use the acronym."
